## qwen-asr — Apache-2.0

Copyright (c) 2026 Alibaba Qwen Team. https://pypi.org/project/qwen-asr/

The model this backend implements. `src/qwen3` is a port to Burn of the
package's `transformers` implementation
(`qwen_asr/core/transformers_backend/modeling_qwen3_asr.py`, version 0.0.6):
the audio encoder, the thinker's text decoder and the splicing of one into the
other. `src/prompt.rs` follows its chat template and its output parsing
(`parse_asr_output`, `detect_and_fix_repetitions`), and `src/audio.rs` its
audio normalization and long-recording split (`normalize_audio_input`,
`split_audio_into_chunks`). This backend ran that package, through PyTorch,
before the port, and `scripts/parity_dump.py` runs it still, as the reference
the port is measured against.


## Burn — MIT / Apache-2.0

Copyright (c) 2022 Burn contributors. https://github.com/tracel-ai/burn

The inference framework, pinned to https://github.com/jorge-menjivar/burn at
revision 9cd83cc49275b12a9ed982e6be921d15f693b24e. The decoder stack in
`src/qwen3/transformer.rs`, the checkpoint adapter in `src/qwen3/mod.rs` and
the model thread in `src/model_thread.rs` are adapted from that revision's
`examples/qwen3-tts`, by way of the Super TTS Qwen TTS backend.


## transformers — Apache-2.0

Copyright (c) 2018 The Hugging Face team. https://github.com/huggingface/transformers

`src/qwen3/audio.rs` computes the log-mel features the way `transformers`'
`WhisperFeatureExtractor` does, and builds its Slaney mel filter bank the way
`transformers.audio_utils.mel_filter_bank` does. `src/prompt.rs` assembles the
Qwen2 tokenizer the way its `Qwen2Converter` does.


## Fetched at runtime, not redistributed here

These are downloaded by the Super STT daemon on the user's machine before first
use, under their own terms; no part of them is contained in this repository or
its release archives.

